OL,3,GNEWSACancer patient wrongly dismissed
OL,4,Aas refusing test
OL,5,
OL,6,FA coroner has raised serious concerns
OL,7,Fafter medical professionals failed to
OL,8,Foffer a woman a test which could have
OL,9,Fdiagnosed her cancer condition sooner.
OL,11,FSunderland coroner Abigail Combes has
OL,12,Fwritten to NHS England following an
OL,13,Finquest for Marie Bell, who died due to
OL,14,Fcomplications during bowel surgery to
OL,15,Fremove a cancerous mass.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,399,390,260,160,0,100
PN,39802
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F398A1788609350
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs1 wsj#57sj  w{j#57i
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$ -,* %-.*,$%** %-& (,,,
OL,3,GNEWSACancer patient wrongly dismissed
OL,4,Aas refusing test
OL,5,
OL,6,FShe said Bell was dismissed as having
OL,7,Fdeclined a colonoscopy which could have
OL,8,Fidentified the mass months earlier,
OL,9,Fmaking surgery less complex. Instead,
OL,10,Fshe had been unable to get into the
OL,11,Fposition required for the test due to
OL,12,Fhip problems.
OL,14,FNHS England said it had systems in
OL,15,Fplace to offer alternative tests to
OL,16,Fcolonoscopy and was working on a review
OL,17,Fwith regional trusts.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
